        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3f42431c-7f5a-5f16-9d83-ec3c8effa2a1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincas Kudirka, Jonas Basanavičius\n- Products: Tautiška giesmė, Lithuanian National Anthem\n- Events: Lithuanian National Revival\n- Concepts: Lithuanian state, Lithuanian people\n\nFacts:\n- Vincas Kudirka was born on 31 December 1858 and died on 16 November 1899.\n- Vincas Kudirka was a Lithuanian poet and physician.\n- Vincas Kudirka wrote both the music and lyrics of the Lithuanian national anthem, \"Tautiška giesmė.\"\n- Tautiška giesmė is the national anthem of Lithuania.\n- Tautiška giesmė is also known by its opening words, \"Lietuva, Tėvyne mūsų,\" and as \"Lietuvos himnas.\"\n- The fifty-word poem of Tautiška giesmė condensed Vincas Kudirka's conceptions of the Lithuanian state, the Lithuanian people, and their past.\n- During the Lithuanian National Revival, Vincas Kudirka and Jonas Basanavičius were among the most active participants.",
